>> title: Mint Chutney
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: indian, mint, cilantro, greens, condiment
>> counters: Curry House, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: mint sauce, hari chutney, pudina chutney, green chutney, mint raita sauce
>> pairs-with: papadom, samosa, seekh-kabab
>> servings: 1 cup
>> time: 15 min
>> step.1: toast 1 min, until it smells of the pan
>> step.2: blend 2 min to a smooth green
>> step.3: whisk in and chill 30 min

Toast @cumin seeds{1%tsp} in a dry #skillet{} ~toast{1%min}, until they darken and smell nutty.

Blend @&(~1)toasted cumin{} with @mint{2%cup}(50 g; leaves only, packed), @cilantro{1%cup}(25 g; stems and all), @green chiles{2}(stemmed), @fresh ginger{1%Tbs}, @lime juice{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @granulated sugar{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} and @ice water{3%Tbs}(45 mL) in a #blender{} ~stir{2%min}, scraping down twice.

Whisk @plain yogurt{1/3%cup}(80 g) into @&(~1)green paste{} and ~chill{30%min}.

Mint stems are bitter and cilantro stems are not. Ice water in the jug or the warm mint goes olive.
